From: CNY Healthcare <cnyhealthymall@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:48:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] docs: bring the guardrail descriptions in line with the
 code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SECURITY.md still advertised the quiet-hours warning and "explicit confirm for
broadcast-to-everyone" — the two claims the preceding commits changed. It also
listed the Quota Guardian as a blast-radius limiter without noting that the
limit was arithmetic on a projected count that broadcast and narrowcast never
supplied.

Updates SECURITY.md, the README feature table, and the three Thai guides so
each states what the code now does: quiet hours refuse a live send, every
uncountable fan-out needs confirm, irreversible tools carry destructiveHint,
and every LINE call runs under a deadline.
